  "interpretation": [
    "The v1 random 128-label draw includes no cold or cut-out examples and omits January and March training months.",
    "There are 3110 exact-zero temperatures among 34360 valid training temperature observations; the lower training quantile is 0°C and the strict-below rule produces only 23 cold target rows. The audit does not determine whether any individual zero temperature is a sensor code or a physical measurement, and no such rows are removed post hoc.",
    "All 134 Q1 validation target rows are wind events, so their validation objective cannot directly assess hot/cold performance. All models must receive the same declared validation labels and search budget.",
    "The Q2 calibration target set has 212 wind and 150 hot examples, with no cold or cut-out examples. Its global conformal radius provides no empirical group-specific cold calibration evidence.",
    "The v1 Full calibration radius is exactly zero because at least the finite-sample rank has score zero; this is not a quantile-rank calculation error.",
    "The new month/event acquisition policy, validation selection, and any other method changes are multiple simultaneous changes. A difference from v1 must not be attributed to one component.",
    "The v1 Q3-Q4 outcomes have already been inspected. A new evaluation on them is a reused-test follow-up, not a new untouched test."
  ]
